      "writtenOn": "2023-11-10T16:05:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As written this will always create new buffers and never use a cached buffer. I think it\u0027s clearer to have an overload of `findOrCreateBuffer` like:\n\n    sk_sp\u003cBuffer\u003e buffer \u003d this-\u003efindOrCreateBuffer(...);\n    DawnBuffer* ptr \u003d static_cast\u003cDawnBuffer*\u003e(buffer.release());\n    return sk_sp\u003cDawnBuffer\u003e(ptr);\n    \nThis way it\u0027s clear that there isn\u0027t anything special happening inside the createDawnBuffer method vs. what happens from the more abstract API.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "b1183f6d4ec96296187229bc8e5a6f5d7cf6f7c1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d9e7ddf_3a392a97",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceProvider.h",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-15T18:34:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we intend to share or cache the DawnBuffer created by createDawnBuffer. This is supposed to be created and used internally by Dawn backend only. For example, the intrinsic constant buffer. It doesn\u0027t need to be cached or ref tracking inside a command buffer, because its content will always be replaced at the beginning of a render pass.\n\nWe need DawnBuffer instead of raw wgpu::Buffer because the former has unique ID which is needed by the BindGroup cache.",
      "parentUuid": "ba10a948_166d749e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "b1183f6d4ec96296187229bc8e5a6f5d7cf6f7c1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
